<title>USA: U.S. to begin open skies talks with Asians Jan 21.</title>
<headline>U.S. to begin open skies talks with Asians Jan 21.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States will begin talks with four Asian nations to lift restrictions on aircraft landing rights, starting with Singapore on January 21 in Washington, Transportation Secretary Federico Pea said Monday.</p>
<p>Discussions to expand access to Malaysia and Taiwan would follow within the next two months, while negotiations with Brunei would take place through the U.S. embassy there, the Transportation Department said.</p>
<p>U.S. officials also expect to continue talks on potential &quot;open skies&quot; agreements with New Zealand and South Korea.  </p>
<p>&quot;This represents an important and concrete step toward our goal of making greater service and enhanced competition a reality over the Pacific, just as it has become in Europe,&quot; Pea said in a statement.</p>
</text>
